Yeah, I did it like this:
let caps=0
print(readline().replace(/[A-Z ]+|[^A-Z]+/g,
  char => {
    if (/[A-Z]/.test(char)) caps = !caps;
    if (caps) return char.toUpperCase()
    else return char.toLowerCase()
  })
)

What made me understand the task was when you said "A BORDER is all typed in with a single shift lock key press". That's because I was parsing individual words at first and ignoring the spaces.

Also, I like that you also said "space isn't affected by shift and thus you don't need to release shift in between". These made the goal extremely clear to me.
